Subject: [PATCH] fix(deps): bump katex to ^0.19.1 to clear CI audit hard gate
 (GHSA-238p-pmpm-9mq7)

Unblocks PR #54: the 'QA dependency audit (hard gate)' step in ci.yml runs
npm audit --package-lock-only --json, which exits non-zero while any advisory
remains. main's lock had katex 0.16.47 (low, prototype pollution, vulnerable
range 0.11.0-0.18.1). Latest 0.16.x is 0.16.47, so no in-range fix exists;
bumped direct dependency to ^0.19.1 (fix version reported by npm audit).

Verification (local, node 22):
- npm audit --package-lock-only --json -> exit 0, 0 vulnerabilities
- npm ci -> ok; tsc -b --noEmit -> ok; vitest -> 515/515 passed; vite build -> ok
- katex has zero imports in src/ (unused direct dep), so runtime impact is nil
